#### Phase 3: Implement Query Side (4 weeks)

**Week 7-8: Read Model and Query Handlers**

1. **Design denormalized read model schema**:

```json
// Elasticsearch member read model (denormalized)
{
  "member_id": "M123456",
  "full_name": "John Doe",
  "date_of_birth": "1980-05-15",
  "eligibility": {
    "status": "active",
    "plan_name": "Gold Plus",
    "effective_date": "2025-01-01",
    "termination_date": null
  },
  "recent_claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM001",
      "service_date": "2025-12-15",
      "provider_name": "City Hospital",
      "amount": 1500.00,
      "status": "approved"
    }
  ],
  "last_updated": "2025-12-26T10:30:00Z"
}
```

1. **Implement query handlers** reading from denormalized store:

```java
@Service
public class MemberQueryHandler {
    private final ElasticsearchOperations elasticsearchOps;
    private final RedisTemplate<String, MemberView> redisCache;

    public MemberView handle(GetMemberQuery query) {
        String cacheKey = "member:" + query.getMemberId();

        // 1. Check cache first (Redis)
        MemberView cached = redisCache.opsForValue().get(cacheKey);
        if (cached != null) {
            return cached; // Cache hit: < 10ms response
        }

        // 2. Query read database (Elasticsearch)
        NativeSearchQuery searchQuery = new NativeSearchQueryBuilder()
            .withQuery(QueryBuilders.matchQuery("member_id", query.getMemberId()))
            .build();

        SearchHit<MemberView> hit = elasticsearchOps
            .searchOne(searchQuery, MemberView.class);

        if (hit == null) {
            throw new MemberNotFoundException(query.getMemberId());
        }

        MemberView member = hit.getContent();

        // 3. Populate cache for future requests (1-hour TTL)
        redisCache.opsForValue().set(cacheKey, member, Duration.ofHours(1));

        return member; // Cache miss: < 50ms response
    }
}
```

**Week 9-10: Event Handlers and Read Model Synchronization**

1. **Implement event handlers** updating read models:

```java
@Service
public class ClaimQueryModelUpdater {
    private final ElasticsearchOperations elasticsearchOps;
    private final RedisTemplate<String, Object> redisCache;

    @KafkaListener(topics = "claims.submitted", groupId = "claim-query-updater")
    public void onClaimSubmitted(ClaimSubmittedEvent event) {
        try {
            // 1. Transform event to read model format
            ClaimReadModel readModel = ClaimReadModel.builder()
                .claimId(event.getClaimId())
                .memberId(event.getMemberId())
                .providerId(event.getProviderId())
                .amount(event.getAmount())
                .status("submitted")
                .submittedAt(event.getTimestamp())
                .build();

            // 2. Upsert to Elasticsearch (idempotent)
            elasticsearchOps.save(readModel);

            // 3. Update member's recent claims in member read model
            updateMemberRecentClaims(event.getMemberId(), readModel);

            // 4. Invalidate cache (optional - can wait for TTL expiration)
            redisCache.delete("member:" + event.getMemberId());

            log.info("Updated claim read model: {}", event.getClaimId());
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Failed to update claim read model: {}", event.getClaimId(), e);
            throw e; // Kafka will retry
        }
    }

    private void updateMemberRecentClaims(String memberId, ClaimReadModel claim) {
        // Update denormalized member document with recent claim
        UpdateQuery updateQuery = UpdateQuery.builder(memberId)
            .withScript("ctx._source.recent_claims.add(params.claim)")
            .withParams(Map.of("claim", claim))
            .build();
        elasticsearchOps.update(updateQuery, MemberReadModel.class);
    }
}
```

1. **Configure Kafka consumers** with appropriate settings:

```yaml
# Spring Boot application.yml
spring:
  kafka:
    consumer:
      group-id: claim-query-updater
      auto-offset-reset: earliest  # Process all events from beginning
      enable-auto-commit: false  # Manual commit after successful processing
      max-poll-records: 100  # Batch processing for efficiency
    listener:
      ack-mode: manual  # Acknowledge only after successful database update
```

